WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.300
Before the world had learned to wake,

2
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:25.880
God spoke a name across the dark —

3
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:32.280
A promise running like a river

4
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:39.520
Through every broken and believing heart.

5
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.540
From Adam's altar to Isaiah,

6
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:52.260
From Simeon's long years at the temple door,

7
00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:00.120
They all kept something they could barely carry

8
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.100
And passed it to the ones who came before.

9
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:14.860
And maybe you know something of that waiting —

10
00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:21.280
The years that no one sees but you and Him.

11
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:27.340
He came for the hidden years.

12
00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:34.740
He came for the ordinary days.

13
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.760
He lived the weight of what you're carrying —

14
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:46.260
Tired hands and grief and unpraised faithfulness.

15
00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:55.200
He came. He came.

16
00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:01.400
Not to the ready and the great —

17
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.640
To Mary's arms and Joseph's hands

18
00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:11.700
And every heart that dared to wait.

19
00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:22.580
Mary said yes before she understood.

20
00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:29.460
Joseph carried shame to shield the one he loved.

21
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:36.800
A refugee child in Egypt, brown-skinned and dependent —

22
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.460
The Son of God learned what it is to need.

23
00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:51.020
For eighteen years, the record holds its silence —

24
00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:57.860
Stone and wood and prayer from dawn until night.

25
00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.520
The parables He told were not invented;

26
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.860
They were things He'd seen with His own eyes.

27
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:17.440
So when He says, "I know your sorrows,"

28
00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:24.140
He knows them from the inside, not above.

29
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:30.620
He came for the hidden years.

30
00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:37.280
He came for the ordinary days.

31
00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.060
He lived the weight of what you're carrying —

32
00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:50.600
Tired hands and grief and unpraised faithfulness.

33
00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:58.480
He came. He came.

34
00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.800
Not to the ready and the great —

35
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.840
To Mary's arms and Joseph's hands

36
00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:15.020
And every heart that dared to wait.

37
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.520
Your hidden years are not a gap,

38
00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.340
The ground for what is building yet.

39
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.580
The preparation was the point —

40
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.560
He never once forgot.

41
00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.860
What promise have you been carrying

42
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.920
Through the seasons no one sees?

43
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:46.000
He named the answer long before you asked,

44
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.600
And He is faithful. He is faithful.

45
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:59.780
He came for the hidden years.

46
00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:06.600
He came for the ordinary days.

47
00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:13.260
He came for you and all your unseen seasons,

48
00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:20.600
And every hidden year. He understands.

49
00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:27.620
He came. He came.

50
00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:31.880
And He is coming still

51
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:37.380
To every heart that dares to wait.

52
00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.060
He always will.

53
00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.880
Wait on the Lord.

54
00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.220
He knows your name.

55
00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.220
He kept His word.
